      "extract": "Introduction Zonal polynomials were introduced by James [Jam60, Jam61] (who credits also Hua [Hua63]) in order to solve some problems from statistics and multivariate analysis. They quickly became a fundamental tool in this theory as well as in the random matrix theory (an overview can be found in the book of Muirhead [Mui82]). They also play an important role in representation theory: they appear as zonal spherical",
